A stored column becomes a generated one of the same name: the ledger drops
the stored one on purpose (its values go), and schema.sql computes it.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, total_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 95, 190);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, total_kr INTEGER GENERATED ALWAYS AS (price_kr * 2)) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN total_kr;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN total_kr;
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, total_kr INTEGER GENERATED ALWAYS AS (price_kr * 2)) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, price_kr
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "price_kr") SELECT "id", "price_kr" FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"

== query
SELECT id, total_kr FROM dish

== rows
1 | 190
